  "display": {
    "name_en": "Fishbone / Ishikawa Diagram",
    "abbr": "",
    "name_zh": "魚骨圖（石川圖）",
    "blurb_en": "Organizes candidate causes of one problem into standard categories (people, process, equipment, materials, environment) branching off a central spine. Use it to brainstorm and categorize causes broadly before narrowing down with Five Whys or Pareto.",
    "blurb_zh": "把一個問題的候選原因，依標準類別（人、流程、設備、物料、環境）分支排列在一條主幹上。想先廣泛腦力激盪、分類原因，再用 Five Whys 或 Pareto 收斂時用。",
    "why_en": "Fishbone can only ever produce a set of HYPOTHESES about the cause, never a confirmed root cause -- the system enforces this structurally: there is no code path that lets a fishbone hypothesis jump straight to a confirmed RootCauseFact, that promotion is refused unless the hypothesis set has actually been run through a real validation method (Five Whys, Pareto, or a causal DAG) first. This stops a good-looking brainstorm from being mistaken for proof.",
    "why_zh": "魚骨圖永遠只能產出一組「假設」，不能直接產出已確認的根因——系統在結構上強制這件事：沒有任何程式路徑能讓魚骨圖的假設直接升級成已確認的 RootCauseFact，除非這組假設真的先跑過一個真正的驗證工具（Five Whys、Pareto，或因果圖），否則升級會被拒絕。這能避免一場好看的腦力激盪被誤認為是證明。",
    "url": "https://asq.org/quality-resources/fishbone"
  },
